{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
From Jeshua the line began to flow
[F]Joia[Bb]kim passed the [C]torch and the robe
[Bb]E[C]liashib stood [Dm]where the altar stood
Joiada [F]served in [C]the [Bb]holy wood
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Recorded [Bb]in the house [Dm]of the [Bb]fathers
Priests and Levites in [F]ancient [C]places
In the days [Dm]of Darius the Persian
[Bb]The names are kept in a [F]holy [C]version
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Jonathan [A7]walked in the priest[Dm]ly path
And Jaddua kept [F]the sa[C]cred oath
[Bb]But one of [C]the sons [Bb]sought a [C]foreign wife
[Dm]Sanballat’s daughter be[F]came his [C]life
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Bb]Recorded [C]in the house [Bb]of the fa[Dm]thers
Priests [Bb]and Levites in ancient [F]places
[C]In the days of Dar[Dm]ius the Persian
The names [Bb]are kept in a holy [F]version
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
Ne[C]hemiah drove the son [A]away
To keep [Bb]the [Bb]covenant clear [F]and [C]bright
The walls [Bb]were [C]rebuilt the spir[Bb]it stayed
[C]Serving [Bb]the Lord with righteous [F][C]light
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Bb]Joiada [C]fathered Jo[Bb]nat[Dm]han
[Bb]Jonathan [F]fathered Jaddua
[C]The line of [Dm]Eliashib stands
{end_of_verse}

